 "text": "Hey there, how are you? Sounds like the chain needs cleaning. A damp rag and a toothbrush usually does the trick. Be careful. It's cheap and easy, but it's also the easiest way to ruin a chain. Only use cooking oil with no additives, and wick it out properly afterwards. Hang the chain off a stand, or get a stand for your workbench. Wipe the chain dry first, then apply a couple of drops of oil. Clean it first. A dirty chain absorbs oil and gets gummy, and that's when squeaks start.",
